## Purpose

Put the same canonical owner information as `work/100k.md` into the hosted project dashboard on a
CEO tab before Overview. Keep the hosted service advisory and read-only while making every
directive actionable through a copyable Tool Shed command that the operator pastes into Codex.

## Settled Direction

- Derive one bounded structured CEO payload from `project_projection.executive()`; never parse the generated Markdown.
- Version the reporter contract and retain compatibility with older reports that lack CEO data.
- Persist the newest per-instance CEO projection without creating hosted lifecycle authority.
- Render all 100k sections on a CEO tab placed before Overview.
- Reuse the existing accessible clipboard control and copy a stable resume command for each directive.
- Stop at a locally verified Work1 commit; do not deploy or report the candidate externally.

## Workstreams

| Workstream | Outcome | Depends On |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Reporter contract | Bounded schema-12 CEO projection derived from canonical 100k truth | project projection |
| Hosted persistence | Per-instance CEO state survives ingest without changing local authority | reporter contract |
| CEO experience | Tab parity, directive commands, responsive layout, and empty/legacy states | hosted persistence |
| Proof | Contract, ingest, view, template, and full validation evidence | prior workstreams |

## Completion Boundary

Complete when the local reporter, ingest model, view context, dashboard template, styles, docs, and
tests prove the CEO tab mirrors the 100k owner surface and copies exact directive resume commands.

